---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHOR_ROLE, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { organizationSchema, breadcrumbSchema, profilePageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { PAGES } from '../../lib/guides';
import { helpers } from '../../lib/helpers';
const lang = 'en';
const h = helpers(lang);
const n = PAGES.length + 1;
---
<PageLayout title="Radif Partners, publisher of US FINRA Exams: who we are" description="Who publishes US FINRA Exams, how its SIE and Series practice questions are written, where every exam format and fee comes from, and what it will never sell." lang={lang} jsonLd={[organizationSchema(lang), profilePageSchema({ path: route('about', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path: route('about', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><p class="kicker">About</p><h1 class="mt-0 text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Who is behind {SITE_NAMES[lang]}</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <div class="not-prose mb-6"><p class="text-lg font-semibold text-navy-900">{AUTHOR_NAME}</p><p class="text-navy-700">{AUTHOR_ROLE[lang]}</p></div>
    <p>{SITE_NAMES[lang]} is published by {AUTHOR_NAME}, a company that builds free tools on public rules and public data. This site is for people preparing the qualification exams of the US securities industry: students and career changers taking the SIE on their own, new hires sitting the Series 7 or Series 6 for their firm, and future advisers facing the Series 63, 65 or 66.</p>
    <h2>What the site does</h2>
    <p>It offers practice by outline section with each answer explained, full mock exams with the official number of questions per section and the official time, and a review mode that brings back the questions you missed. Around the exams, it works out which exams a job needs, what they cost in 2026, when a failed exam can be retaken, when an enrollment window closes and how long a pass stays valid. Everything is free, without an account or an email address; progress stays in your browser.</p>
    <h2>Where the questions and rules come from</h2>
    <p>We wrote all {h.num(h.count)} practice questions ourselves, each from a topic of the public content outlines that FINRA and NASAA publish. Their text is not reproduced, and we never present our questions as real exam questions. Formats, fees and rules were read on finra.org, in FINRA's rulebook and fee schedule and in the NASAA study guides, and every page links to the official page behind it. The <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a> explains how a mock is drawn and marked.</p>
    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <p>We are not FINRA, NASAA, Prometric, a state securities regulator, a broker-dealer or a training company. We cannot enroll you, schedule an exam, see a score report or sponsor a registration. The site uses no official logo or seal.</p>
    <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
    <p>The site sells no course, book or flash cards, takes no commission and links to no firm that does. If advertising is added one day, it will never sit inside a quiz, and it cannot use your answers, which never leave your browser.</p>
    <h2>Tell us when something is wrong</h2>
    <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the rule, or the first words of the question. The <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a> explains how a correction is made and dated. The site has {n} pages.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600">Formats and fees last checked on <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-US')}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
